{"content":[{"c":["ASHTAROTH, ASHTERATHITE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Town of Bashan, named along with Edrei as the home of King Og (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.1.4","r":"Deut.1.4","rawR":"Deut.1.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.1.4","value":"Deut.1.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 1:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.9.10","r":"Josh.9.10","rawR":"Josh.9.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.9.10","value":"Josh.9.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 9:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.12.4","r":"Josh.12.4","rawR":"Josh.12.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.12.4","value":"Josh.12.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.12,31","r":"Josh.13.12,31","rawR":"Josh.13.12,31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.12,31","value":"Josh.13.12,31"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:12, 31"},"). Ashtaroth is the plural form of Ashtoreth, the name of the Canaanite fertility goddess who was worshiped there. After Og was defeated by the Israelites (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.1-11","r":"Deut.3.1-11","rawR":"Deut.3.1-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.1-11","value":"Deut.3.1-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:1-11"},"), Moses gave Ashtaroth to the half-tribe of Manasseh (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.12,31","r":"Josh.13.12,31","rawR":"Josh.13.12,31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.12,31","value":"Josh.13.12,31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:12, 31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.13","r":"Deut.3.13","rawR":"Deut.3.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.13","value":"Deut.3.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:13"},"). Later, it became a Levitical city inhabited by the Gershonites (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.71","r":"1Chr.6.71","rawR":"1Chr.6.71","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.71","value":"1Chr.6.71"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:71"},"). Ashteroth-karnaim (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.5","r":"Gen.14.5","rawR":"Gen.14.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.5","value":"Gen.14.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:5"},") is probably the same town as Ashtaroth. Its location is usually identified with Tell Ashtarah, 21 miles (34 kilometers) east of the Sea of Galilee. In ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.44","r":"1Chr.11.44","rawR":"1Chr.11.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.44","value":"1Chr.11.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 11:44"}," one of David’s mighty men, Uzzia, is called an Ashterathite."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AshtarothAshterathite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 1:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.1.4","rawQueryValue":"Deut.1.4","sourceRefExact":"Deut.1.4"},{"anchorText":"Jos 9:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.9.10","rawQueryValue":"Josh.9.10","sourceRefExact":"Josh.9.10"},{"anchorText":"12:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.12.4","rawQueryValue":"Josh.12.4","sourceRefExact":"Josh.12.4"},{"anchorText":"13:12, 31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.12,31","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.12,31","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.12,31"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:1-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.1-11","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.1-11","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.1-11"},{"anchorText":"Jos 13:12, 31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.12,31","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.12,31","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.12,31"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.13","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.13","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:71","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.71","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.71","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.71"},{"anchorText":"Gn 14:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 11:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.44","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.44","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.44"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ab1204db105d8643d033d39814e24eac2dd88c603585a86c5430554b62ecf2a0","sourceItemName":"AshtarothAshterathite","sourceItemOrder":550,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AshtarothAshterathite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ashtaroth, Ashterathite*","title":"Ashtaroth, Ashterathite*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}